t} jumps to reach 0\",\n  \"{actor} solved this problem: \\\"{problem}\\\" {actor} says the answer is {answer}. Is {actor} correct?\",\n  \"{actor} solved: \\\"{problem}\\\". {actor} says the {miss} is {answer}. Is {actor} correct?\",\n  \"{q} The answer is {v}.\",\n  \"{statement}. True or False?\",\n  \"There are {a} {objects}. If {b} {objects} are put in each bag, how many bags are needed?\",\n  \"{actor} wants to share {a} {objects} equally among {b} friends. How many {objects} does each friend get?\"\n ],\n \"overall\": \"FAIL\",\n \"reasoning\": \"Divisor out of scope (F04, F05, F06, F07, F08, F09, F12): the competency names the 2, 3, 4, 5, and 10 tables and the lc declares table 2_3_4_5_10, but the divisor slots print 8. F04, F06 and F07 print b with printed_runs \\\"2 to 5, 8, 10\\\", and F05, F08 and F09 print b or divisor with printed_runs \\\"3, 8\\\". The 8 is observed in rendered values, so these are not hypothetical. F12 fails because it nests F09. Objects outside the grade and the vocabulary a grade 2 learner can read (F15, F17): OBJECTS_POOL, which F15 and F17 print through their objects slot, contains items such as \\\"gacha tickets\\\", \\\"lightsticks\\\", \\\"photocards\\\", \\\"donation cards\\\", \\\"ballot papers\\\", \\\"campaign posters\\\" and \\\"speech scripts\\\", and \\\"gacha\\\" and \\\"lightsticks\\\" are words a grade 2 learner cannot read. F15 and F17 are the faulty families; F11, F13 and F14 fail because they print F17, F15 and F13 text. Note, not a basis for failing: F13 and F14 join as \\\"{q} The answer is {v}.\\\" followed by \\\"{statement}. True or False?\\\", which prints a double period after the answer. Templates F01, F02, F03, F10 and F16 pass: their gated words and names are in scope, and F16 prints no objects. Judged on the packet alone; no seed was printed in it, so none is cited.\"\n}",
